      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Pro-voucher advocates often ignore the cost gap because they believe the market will naturally correct it through increased demand from wealthier families, which they argue will eventually force private schools to lower prices. However, critics are right that without full funding, vouchers function as a subsidy for the wealthy while leaving the public system to absorb the financial strain of the poorest students. This creates a two-tier system where the program's success is measured by the ability of the rich to opt out, rather than the ability of the poor to access quality education.",
